# infra/terraform/railway/.env.example  (TRACKED — keys only, no values)
#
# Copy to  infra/terraform/railway/.env  (git-ignored) and fill in real values.
# This file holds ONLY the bootstrap credentials the Terraform providers /
# remote backend need — every other value (service variable, GitHub secret)
# lives in  secrets/{shared,staging,production}.tfvars.
#
# Loaded by the `make terraform-*` targets (see Makefile's TF_ENV_FILE) and,
# for the two RAILWAY_TOKEN_* below, by scripts/pull_railway_variables.py.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# HCP Terraform API token — the remote backend (app.terraform.io) that stores
# state. The Makefile / .github/workflows/terraform.yml re-export this as
# TF_TOKEN_app_terraform_io (the name the `cloud {}` block actually reads).
# In CI: GitHub Actions secret  TF_API_TOKEN.
TF_API_TOKEN=

# GitHub PAT for the `github` provider — writes the Actions secrets/variables
# github-ci.tf manages (repo admin: Secrets + Variables). MUST be dedicated —
# not a token reused by any other CI step (RELEASE_PAT / NPM_TOKEN / ...).
# Re-exported as GITHUB_TOKEN and TF_VAR_github_token.
# In CI: GitHub Actions secret  TF_GITHUB_TOKEN.
TF_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# (removed) RAILWAY_TOKEN — was the account-level token for the community
# `railway` Terraform provider, gone since Revision 4. `railway up` /
# `railway config` use a project token; see RAILWAY_TOKEN_<ENV> below.

# Railway PROJECT tokens, one per environment — used by `make railway-config-*`
# (`.railway/railway.ts` + `railway config`). `railway config` has no
# `--environment` flag, so the token itself selects the env. Same token as the
# `scraper / <env>` GitHub Environment's `secrets.RAILWAY_TOKEN`
# (`gh_env_railway_token` in secrets/github-<env>.tfvars).
RAILWAY_TOKEN_STAGING=
RAILWAY_TOKEN_PRODUCTION=
